{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>On the day. You shall flourish.</b> From the root שגיא (Job 36:26): you shall make it great swiftly. Similarly: ובבקר זרעך תפריחי. And behold, I tell you a general principle regarding the words of the prophets of rebuke: from half the verse we learn about its other half, in most cases." "<b>A harvest heap.</b> And behold, ינוד הקציר — like וטל ילין בקצירי (Job 29:19)." "<b>On the day of inheritance.</b> מכה is missing. And behold, נחלה is a descriptor of blow, and similarly מאכלו בריאה (Habakkuk 1:16). And the proof: וכאב אנוש, from the root of ויאנש (II Samuel 12:15). And behold, the meaning is: you multiplied children, and the day of calamity came, and they ceased."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:54:10.609966718Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}